## Acceptance Criteria (per-plan, testable)

1. `ProjectPMConfig.statuses` declares all 9 canonical CASCADE stage keys (optional), verifiable by the type-level test and by grep.
2. Every key in `STATUS_TO_AGENT` is present as a key of `ProjectPMConfig.statuses`.
3. `LinearIntegration.resolveLifecycleConfig` passes 8 keys through (no `debug`), verifiable by unit test.
4. `JiraIntegration.resolveLifecycleConfig` passes 8 keys through, verifiable by unit test.
5. `LINEAR_STATUS_SLOTS` contains exactly the 8 stages in lifecycle order, and the Linear Field Mapping step renders 8 rows (verifiable by SSR test).
6. The Linear wizard does not render a `debug` row.
7. Saving a Linear integration with any subset of the 8 mappings persists exactly those mappings (no dropped keys, no extra keys), verifiable by integration test against the existing `projects.integrations.upsert` path.
8. A Linear webhook transitioning to a state mapped to `splitting` / `planning` / `todo` / `merged` dispatches the corresponding agent.
9. A JIRA webhook transitioning to a state mapped to `splitting` / `planning` / `todo` dispatches the corresponding agent.
10. A transition to an unmapped state returns no agent dispatch and produces no error.
11. The Trello Field Mapping step renders byte-identically to its pre-spec state (diff-in-HTML assertion).
12. The JIRA Field Mapping step's rendered UI is unchanged (diff-in-HTML assertion).
13. A pre-spec Linear integration (4 mappings set) opened in the wizard after the change renders the 4 pre-existing mappings populated and the 4 new slots empty; saving without filling them does not drop the 4 pre-existing mappings.
14. All new / modified code has corresponding tests.
15. `npm run build` passes.
16. `npm test` passes.
17. `npm run test:integration` passes.
18. `npm run lint` passes.
19. `npm run typecheck` (root) and `cd web && npx tsc -b` (web) pass.
20. `CHANGELOG.md` has the parity entry under `## Unreleased`.

